    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Turns HTML character references such as &amp;, &eacute; and &#163; in a text field back into the characters they stand for, in a new field.",
    "category": "Preparation",
    "subcategory": null,
    "tags": [
        "html",
        "escape",
        "unescape",
        "entities",
        "decode",
        "text cleaning"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Text taken from web pages, feeds, CMS exports or APIs often carries HTML character references: `&amp;` for &, `&eacute;` for é, `&#163;` for £, `&nbsp;` for a non-breaking space. This block turns them back into the characters they stand for, in a new field.\n\n**How to set it up**: choose the text field and a name for the new field (use the same name to replace it).\n\n- **Repeat for double-escaped text**: tick when the text was escaped twice (`&amp;lt;` should become `<`).\n- **Non-breaking spaces as plain spaces**: ticked by default, so `&nbsp;` becomes an ordinary space that matches in joins and filters.\n\nHTML tags such as `<b>` are not removed, and text that is not a known reference (`R&D`, `Q&A`) is left as it is. Missing values stay missing.",
    "dependencies": "",
    "options": [
        {
            "name": "fieldName",
            "title": "Text to unescape",
            "description": "The text field holding the escaped text.",
            "groupTitle": null,
